    endurance vs. perdurance
        | here endurance is better explained as a matter of perdurance
            | ∵ a longer endurance (as here) calls for a fuller explanans
                ∵ a longer endurance in the explanandum makes the chancier,
                  more contingent explanantia less convincing
                    ∵ longer endurance by chance is more improbable, more surprising
                ∵ full explanans(endurance(⁠m⁠)) = explanans(perdurance(⁠m⁠))
                    : ad `full explanans` : explanans that is true necessarily,
                      as opposed to contingently, such as a theoretic ground
                    ⁠m⁠: a mortal, a thing prone to existential hazard
                ? extreme endurance → perdurance, how (precisely) form that inference?
                    : join @ `^*- the endurance/perdurance given is that of.+mundane design`s
                    - crucially the inference is valid in contexts of explanation,
                      though not in contexts of fact
                        + try deferring the inference till the issue is one of explanation
                          as opposed to fact
                        + re-ask the question then
            | ∵ in weighty matters, reason’s discontent comes to the fore and prods us
              ever onward to the fullest explanation, such as a ground
                : cf. notepad:2026-10-12c : relating as equivalents (i) brute fact and
                  (ii) the non-existence of a stable ground, each being a null explanans
                  or case of groundlessness, either of (i) theory or (ii) practice
                !! weak, unconvincing
        | what inherently is indefinitely, open-endedly endurant must be perdurant in aim
            - the only way to aim at indefinite, open-ended endurance, is to aim at perdurance
                ∵ the former includes a potential for the latter and the latter has necessary conditions
            !! no such inherence is given by the explanans (mundane design)
                - it depends on the (ungiven, indeterminate) reason *had* by the cosmocrafters
            ? extreme endurance → perdurance, how (precisely) form that inference?
                : join @ `^*- the endurance/perdurance given is that of.+mundane design`s
                ?+ is it still a problem in this context?
